work=ph("Our Work","Projects, tools and innovations from the field.","Portfolio")+f'''
<section class="sec" id="wsp"><div class="wrap"><span class="tag">Viega Project · In progress</span><h2>Water Security Plan, Bakshi Ka Talab, Lucknow</h2><p class="lead">Commissioned by WaterAid India with Jal Seva Charitable Foundation. Work Order JSCF/UP/IN158/WO/2026-27/58, 28 August 2026.</p>
<div class="stats" style="margin-top:34px;border-radius:20px"><div class="wrap g" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)"><div><b data-count="19">0</b><span>Wards</span></div><div><b data-count="40">0</b><span>Habitations</span></div><div><b data-count="71200">0</b><span>Population</span></div></div></div>
<h3 style="margin-top:50px">Our approach: community insight with technical excellence</h3><div class="steps"><div class="step rv"><h3>Participatory water budgeting</h3><p>Engaging communities and understanding shared priorities.</p></div><div class="step rv d1"><h3>Technical analysis</h3><p>Data-driven assessment of groundwater resources, quality, demand and risks.</p></div><div class="step rv d2"><h3>Plan and action roadmap</h3><p>Prioritised interventions and a 20-year implementation pathway.</p></div></div>
<h3 style="margin-top:50px">What the plan delivers</h3><div class="grid g4"><div class="card rv"><div class="n">01</div><h3>Ward-level plans</h3><p>Plans for all 19 wards, built on community consultation.</p></div><div class="card rv d1"><div class="n">02</div><h3>Consolidated town plan</h3><p>One actionable framework bringing every ward together.</p></div><div class="card rv d2"><div class="n">03</div><h3>Assessment and consultation</h3><p>Situation assessment, field engagement and stakeholder consultation.</p></div><div class="card rv d3"><div class="n">04</div><h3>Institutional framework</h3><p>Clear roles and a delivery pathway for the Nagar Panchayat and partners.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="sec alt"><div class="wrap split"><div class="rv l"><span class="tag">Capacity building</span><h2>Research-based training for Urban Local Bodies</h2><p class="lead">Evidence-backed, field-informed content developed for the resource person at the Dr. Raghunandan Singh Tolia Uttarakhand Academy of Administration (ATI), Nainital.</p>
<p><b>For:</b> mayors, chairpersons, executive officers, sanitary and field inspectors and other ULB officials.</p><ul class="tick"><li>Policy and regulatory framework</li><li>SWM systems and best practices</li><li>Planning, finance and service delivery</li><li>Case studies and field insights</li><li>Community engagement and behaviour change</li></ul></div><div class="rv r"><img src="assets/trainA.png" alt="Training session for urban local bodies"><img src="assets/trainB.png" alt="Training materials" style="margin-top:20px"></div></div></section>
<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><p class="eyebrow">Track record</p><h2>Selected projects and case studies</h2><div class="grid g4">
<div class="card rv"><div class="n" style="font-size:2.4rem">9.3%</div><h3>Emissions reduction</h3><p>Cradle-to-gate LCA of fly-ash bricks for a Bangalore-based client found a lower-carbon formulation with improved strength.</p></div>
<div class="card rv d1"><div class="n" style="font-size:2.4rem">15–20%</div><h3>Efficiency target</h3><p>Deep-learning surrogate model with IIT Roorkee to speed CFD prediction of RDF combustion in waste-to-energy boilers.</p></div>
<div class="card rv d2"><div class="n" style="font-size:2.4rem">63%</div><h3>Thickness reduction</h3><p>ML-based CBR and pavement prediction for geosynthetic-reinforced expansive soils.</p></div>
<div class="card rv d3"><div class="n" style="font-size:2.4rem">2030</div><h3>National outlook</h3><p>Projection of urban India's MSW, GHG emissions and Bio-CNG potential under SBM-U 2.0.</p></div></div>
<div class="grid g3"><div class="card rv"><span class="tag">Water and sanitation</span><h3>Wastewater treatment</h3><p>Activated carbon and chitosan-coated bentonite achieving 86–95% removal of lead, chromium, mercury, COD and BOD.</p></div><div class="card rv d1"><span class="tag">Circular economy</span><h3>Biochar</h3><p>Biochar from rice husk, neem leaves and sludge, with LCA-based GHG offset analysis.</p></div><div class="card rv d2"><span class="tag">Climate and air</span><h3>Heat and pollution</h3><p>PM₂.₅ as a co-indicator of heat–pollution vulnerability in Vijayawada, with a policy-gap review.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="sec alt"><div class="wrap"><div class="grid g2" style="margin:0"><div class="card rv"><span class="tag">Patent filed</span><h3>Modular Waste Collection Vehicle</h3><p>Adjustable bin compartments based on community segregation levels, supporting source segregation, modular design for different communities and cleaner cities. Inventor: Dr. Abhay Kumar Verma (Principal Investigator). Application No. 202611118413, filed 3 October 2026, Indian Patent Office, New Delhi.</p><img src="assets/truck.png" alt="Modular waste collection vehicle" style="margin-top:18px;border-radius:12px"></div>
<div class="card rv d1"><span class="tag">Digital tool</span><h3>SWM Logbook Generator</h3><p>A bilingual web tool that generates 30-day, audit-ready Excel logbooks for ULB, MRF and mixed-waste facilities.</p><ul class="tick"><li>Gate intake from population or actual TPD, with seasonal variation</li><li>MRF sorting with custom fractions that always sum to 100%</li><li>Processing and rejects balanced against intake</li></ul><p style="margin-top:18px"><a class="btn dark" href="https://swm-standalone-tool.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the tool</a></p></div></div></div></section>'''
